## What a `type: markdown-meta-type` instance is

**The default meta-type** for the corpus.  Memorials under this meta-type are stored as markdown files with YAML frontmatter, under the `memory/` subtree, and accessed through the standard memorial-system CLI surface.

Every existing type memorial in a sandbar-backed corpus (decision, plan, library, predicate, observation, ...) implicitly uses `markdown-meta-type` as its meta-type.  The `has-meta-type:` typed-edge is OMITTABLE on type memorials that follow this default; absence of the edge implies `markdown-meta-type`.

Markdown-Meta-Type is a subtype of [`meta-type`](meta-type.md) → [`meta`](meta.md).

## Substrate

- **Storage**: markdown files (`*.md`) under the corpus subtree
- **Format**: YAML frontmatter + markdown body
- **Schema authority**: `types/<name>.md` memorials declare what fields each `type:` requires + recommends; `predicates/<name>.md` memorials declare what typed-edge predicates exist + their domain/range
- **Versioning**: git (every commit captures a snapshot)

## Access surface

| Concern | Tool / surface |
|---|---|
| Full-text search | `/memory-search` (BM25F over name / description / tags / body / path) |
| Single memorial view | `/memory-show <rel-path>` |
| Subtree listing | `/memory-tree <path>` |
| Type catalog | `/memory-type-tree` |
| Typed-edge walks | `/memory-search --from <slug> --via <path-expr>` |
| Library Card view | `/memory-library-card <rel>` |
| Aggregation | `/memory-search --aggregate count --group-by ...` |

